 34K  c  2024Dr01: a 72-MeV/nucleon {+37}Ca secondary beam was produced via the 
 34K 2c  fragmentation of a 140-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca{+20+} primary beam impinging
 34K 3c  on a 0.5-mm-thick Be target. Experimental setup includes the           
 34K 4c  CAESium-iodide scintillator ARray (CAESAR) for detecting |g rays, a    
 34K 5c  DSSD-CsI(Tl) |DE-E Ring Telescope for detecting protons, a             
 34K 6c  Scintillating-Fiber Array (SFA) and the S800 spectrograph for detecting
 34K 7c  heavy residuals. Measured E{-p}, E|g, and E(residual). Deduced levels, 
 34K 8c  mass excess from total decay-energy spectra using the invariant-mass   
 34K 9c  method. Comparisons with shell-model calculations with the USDC        
 34K Ac  Hamiltonian.                                                           
